From 150990af6e2cabf46f060250c2974f1b28269c0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michal Frdlik <michaelf.ms@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 15:45:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] Thylacine Warp vkQuake-arc W-1: offscreen pipeline
 witness + F9 mem-reclaim convergence

The multi-queue chunk left four items tracked to the vkQuake arc's first
sub-chunk (W-1, operator-voted 2026-08-26). This lands the mesa half of
three, plus the first pipeline-class traffic through the venus transport.

thylacine_prove.c (test only) gains three witness steps:
  - Step 6b: the F3 two-timeline interleave. Fenced pattern copies on two
    logical devices (V3D is 1 queue family x 1 queue, so timeline 2 is only
    reachable via a second logical device), waited in REVERSE submit order.
    The multi-queue chunk shipped the per-timeline retirement arithmetic
    sound-by-POLICY (the copy proof rode one timeline; the lift leg never
    submitted); this makes it sound-by-WITNESS -- a misrouted retirement
    leaves the stranded lane's timeline ledger short and its park unfillable
    (a hang caught by the gate timeout).
  - Step 8: the offscreen SPIR-V triangle -- the FIRST render-pass / pipeline
    / draw traffic through venus (everything prior is transfer-class). A
    64x64 R8G8B8A8 attachment is cleared blue, an embedded triangle is
    rasterized red, the attachment is copied to a host-visible buffer, and
    BOTH pixel classes are asserted (center red AND corner blue -- the pair
    is the control: all-red = clear lost, all-blue = draw lost).
  - Step 9: the discriminating slot-exhaustion witness. Step 7's 3-slot cap
    cycle cannot see a burned handle in a 256-slot space (the tracked F2
    gap). Allocate 4 KiB memories until refusal, three cycles with full frees
    between; cycles 2 and 3 must refuse at EQUAL counts.

warp_client.c: the F9 convergence. warp_mem_new's maybe-installed failure arm
(-EINTR maybe-commits, info-read failures, and E_IO device faults under
GLOBAL hostmem pressure -- the tracked F9 wedge) previously kept the handle
marked, a bounded leak a cross-client E_IO loop could drive to the 256-slot
ceiling. It now resolves the ambiguity with a best-effort mem/<handle>/ctl
destroy (warp_mem_reclaim): a full write confirms teardown, -ENOENT asserts
absence, either freeing the handle; only a reclaim whose own transport fails
keeps it. The duplicate -EINVAL arm NEVER reclaims -- there the slot is a
live earlier mint, and a destroy would tear down real memory (the ring-F1
wedge's data-loss twin). ENOENT==2 pinned kernel-registry == p9::E_NOENT ==
musl sysroot. Scoped to the conn's own ctx, under the transport mutex.

vn_renderer_thylacine.c: comment only.

Every graphics entrypoint the prove adds is a defined T symbol in
libvulkan_virtio.a (nm census -- the loader-less direct-symbol link holds).
Built clean on thyla-keep; witnessed GREEN on thyla-pi/KVM real V3D 4.2.14
(offscreen triangle center-red/corner-blue, two-timeline interleave, slot-
exhaustion 255/255/255, PASS).

Audit (holotype-reviewer Fable 5 max, MODEL start==end, the F9 device-memory
surface / I-45): 0 P0 / 0 P1 / 0 P2 / 4 P3 -- CLEAN. Three P3s were
comment-accuracy fixes folded into this commit (F1 the reclaim open-leg
-ENOENT is kernel-manufactured hence best-effort, residue bounded +
self-healing; F2 a stale sibling doc block; F4 a misroute is a park-hang not
a 10 s FAIL). F3 (the reclaim path has no discriminating witness) stays
OWED -- a test-mode mem-inject lever is the follow-on. All three fixes are
comment-only, so the witnessed binary is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
